Here is a simple implementation of a function that returns all prime numbers up to a given integer `n` in Go:

```
func primeNumbers(n int) []int {
    primes := []int{2}
    for i := 3; i <= n; i++ {
        for _, p := range primes {
            if i%p == 0 {
                break
            }
        }
        primes = append(primes, i)
    }
    return primes
}
```

This function uses a simple algorithm called trial division, which checks whether each number up to `n` is divisible by any of the prime numbers found so far. If a number is divisible, it is added to the list of prime numbers.
