Sure! Here's a simple bubble sorting algorithm:
1. Create an array of items to be sorted.
2. Set two pointers, one starting at the beginning of the array and the other starting at the end.
3. Compare the values of the two pointers. If they are different, swap the values of the pointers.
4. Repeat steps 2 and 3 until the pointers are at the end of the array.
5. At this point, the values in the middle of the array are in sorted order.
6. Repeat steps 2-5 until the end of the array has been reached.
7. The sorted array is now complete.
Here's some sample code to illustrate the algorithm:

```css
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    int i, j, temp;
    for (i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
        for (j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
                temp = arr[j];
                arr[j] = arr[j+1];
                arr[j+1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This code sorts an array of integers in ascending order.

